<<~ ahu #/head>>

! The True Name model ~ three parts that bind without merging

A device holds an Ed25519 keypair minted where it stands. A human holds a persona root of their own.
An edge joins them and keeps them apart.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-three-parts>>

!! Three parts, and each answers for something different

# ''The VESSEL key belongs to the PLACE.'' Founding mints it per-install off the local CSPRNG, it
persists owner-only on that disk, and ''it NEVER travels to another vessel.'' It names a somewhere,
and it signs only AS ITSELF.
# ''The PERSONA ROOT belongs to the HUMAN.'' A DISTINCT key in its own slot — never derived from the
vessel seed, never the same bytes, never copied outward.
# ''The DELEGATION EDGE binds the two without collapsing them.'' The persona root signs that an
operator delegates to a device AT A PLACE, and the hearth's True Name rides in that statement. ''The
edge IS the relationship'', and the vessel's stack holds it as a capability rather than as an
identity.

The three read as a stack of capabilities on a nameless entity — never as a numbered plane, and never
as one key wearing three hats.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/why-the-split-carries-weight>>

!! What one key would cost

''A single key copied across a person's vessels presents the SAME collector to every verifier.'' One
bit then links every self they hold — every handle, every circle, every face — and no policy above
that layer can unlink them again.

Holding the vessel apart from the persona makes the veil, the PersonaGroup and the Handle
architecture implementable at all. ''The separation does not harden a design that would otherwise
work; it decides whether the design exists.''

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/law>>

!! The lifecycle invariants

# ''The keypair generates DEVICE-LOCAL and persists owner-only.'' Nothing mints it elsewhere and
carries it in.
# ''The verifying key feeds `did:key`, and the DERIVATION happens in the TW5 VM.'' The cold-boot
ceremony owns that step, so the naming rite stays inside the wiki rather than in host code.
# ''A display name derives from LOCAL truth.'' It reads the operator's own git config and makes no
network call, so opening a vessel asks nobody's permission to know what to call itself.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/edges>>

